  "Description": {
    "Cost": 31095471,
    "UIName": "Ophanim",
    "Id": "chassisdef_ophanim_C-OPM-O",
    "Name": "Ophanim",
    "Details": "The Invictus is the primary configuration of the Ophanim, meant as the assault shock troopers of a Level II formation. Bringing four Heavy PPC, each with an attached capacitor, and two MRM-30 launchers to the battlefield. Relying on its raw attack power the configuration does mount less armor than expected of a Superheavy, but the strengthening traits of the Sanctus armor compensates to some degree. \n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Divine Fortress</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.29</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Omni</color>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_ophanim"
  },
  "VariantName": "C-OPM-O",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitUpperLeft",
      "ArmLimitUpperRight",
      "OmniMech",
      "Superheavy",
      "mr-resize-1.21"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Celestial Superheavy",
  "YangsThoughts": "The Ophanim was created by the Word of Blake to become the keystone of their blessed military forces. Weighting in at 150t and utilizing a 425-rated core, the Ophanim brings Divine Wrath in its arms, and the Blessed Rains in the side torsos.  Those hoping that great weight given to the weaponry has cost it armor protection, will find that the Spirit of Blake has been blessed on this Sanctus Armor, helping to lift the load from those going to preach the Truth under fire.  Included as well, is a Blessed Gyro, and Seraphim EWAR Suite, both given blessings by the highest priests of the order, which has had some positive effects on combat performance. And to drive home the point that this is a model just for those who truly believe, it requires the pilot to have undergone significant cyberfication, to the point of almost embedding them into the cockpit.",
